<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isaac Komnenos of Cyprus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1155–1196</span> · Also known as Isaac Comnenus of Cyprus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isaac Komnenos was a Byzantine aristocrat and great-nephew of Emperor Manuel I who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> in 1184 and ruled it as a self-proclaimed emperor. His harsh rule ended when Richard the Lionheart, on his way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, conquered the island in 1191. Richard sold Cyprus to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a> and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isaac-komnenos-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="Isaac Komnenos of Cyprus" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown / Photography: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tetarteron,_Byzantine,_Isaac_Comnenus,_1185-1191.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
